-- title:
--   First-order action of a relabelling on Drinfeld origin parameters
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$, a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$, and a commutative ring $A_0$ in which $\ell_g$ is invertible (`hℓA`).
--
--   Three transport hypotheses feed the construction of the rigid Weierstrass datum. The hypothesis `hℓ` states that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData` $D = (x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$ over $T$, if $D$ is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $W$ — that is, $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the affine equation of $W$, $(W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi\,\ell_g)(x_P)=0$, $x_Q=x_P$ and $y_Q=y_P$ — then the transformed datum `D.variableChange C` is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point of $C \bullet W$. The hypothesis `hM` states that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` is carried to `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k (kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h)`. The hypothesis `hL` states that divisibility $h \mid$ `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` implies `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h ∣ inLineMulPoly (C • W) ℓg n (u_C^{-2}(x - r_C))`. Further data are a family of relative group laws $\mathcal G$ on projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras, assumed chord–tangent (`h𝒢`: each law admits a points evaluation) and origin-normalised (`h𝒢O`: the identity section is cut out by an origin chart $\chi$ with $\chi(x/y)=\chi(z/y)=0$), together with a level transport $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport` (`h𝒯`: the sections of $\mathcal T$-transported Drinfeld pairs are the pullbacks of the original sections along the graded maps realising variable changes, respectively coefficient maps).
--
--   The rigid datum is `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`. Its raw objects over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ consist of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with a level structure in three slots: a family $(h_p)$ indexed by the prime factors $p$ of $M'$ with `IsGamma0PowAt` at $(p, v_p(M'))$; a `LevelPData` which is a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point; and a `RawDrinfeldPair` (a projective Weierstrass curve with two sections $P$, $Q$) which is of level $q$ for $\mathcal G$; subject to the link condition `IsGamma1Link`, namely that $h_{\ell_g}$ divides `inLineMulPoly W ℓg (ℓg ^ (M'.factorization ℓg - 1)) x_P`. Its points `Pt T` are the raw objects modulo the variable-change relation. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` supply, for each variable change $C$ of a projective curve $W$ and each $A_0$-algebra map $f$, a graded ring homomorphism between the projective-model gradings whose irrelevant ideal condition holds and which is a variable-change homomorphism, respectively a coefficient homomorphism, in the explicit sense of `IsVariableChangeHom` and `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   Let $P_0$ be a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for the associated level moduli datum: a commutative $A_0$-algebra $B_0 = P_0.B_0$ with a point `P₀.univ` over it such that every point over every $A_0$-algebra is the image of `P₀.univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra map; `P₀.classify y` denotes that unique map for a point $y$. Let $x$ be a raw object over $B_0$ whose class is `P₀.univ` (`hx`).
--
--   The deformation-theoretic frame is as follows. $R$ is a noetherian local domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, an $A_0$-algebra, with an $A_0$-algebra map $\iota : B_0 \to R$; $k$ is a field of characteristic $q$ in which $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are nonzero (`hℓk`, `hM'k`); $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ is surjective with kernel $\mathfrak m_R$; $W_0$ is a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain with maximal ideal generated by $q$ (`hW₀`) and a surjection $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ with kernel its maximal ideal; $R$ is a $W_0$-algebra, $W_0$ an $A_0$-algebra, the scalar towers agree, and $\mathrm{res}_R$ restricted to $W_0$ is $\mathrm{res}_0$ (`hresR₀`). The hypothesis `hfac` is the representability of $R$ on artinian test objects: for every artinian local $W_0$- and $A_0$-algebra $T$ with compatible towers and every surjection $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ with kernel $\mathfrak m_T$ extending $\mathrm{res}_0$, each $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi : B_0 \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_R \circ \iota$ extends to a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\Phi : R \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \Phi = \mathrm{res}_R$ and $\Phi \circ \iota = \varphi$.
--
--   Formal-group data: $F$ is a commutative formal group over $R$ whose power series is the fixed formal group law of the curve in the Drinfeld-pair slot `level.2.2.curve` of `mapRing ι x` (`hFW`); $F_0$ is a commutative formal group over $k$ whose power series is that of the reduction of the same curve along $\mathrm{res}_R$ (`hF₀W`), and $F_0$ satisfies `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. with respect to the zero ideal its $q$-th series is a unit power series times its Drinfeld divisor at the parameters $0,0$. The hypothesis `hssJ` states that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring map $\iota_\Omega : k \to \Omega$, the image of $\mathrm{res}_R(\iota(P_0.j_0))$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point; here $P_0.j_0$ is the element of $B_0$ recording the $j$-invariant of the universal point.
--
--   Let $\chi_P, \chi_Q$ be ring homomorphisms from the origin chart ring of `((…).mapRing ι x).level.2.2.curve` to $R$ such that the sections $P$ and $Q$ of that Drinfeld pair reduce to the origin with respect to them and $\mathfrak m_R$ (`hP`, `hQ`: each $\chi$ is an origin chart section for the corresponding section and both `originParam χ` $= -\chi(x/y)$ and `originW χ` lie in $\mathfrak m_R$). Write $x_0 =$ `originParam χP` and $x_1 =$ `originParam χQ`. It is assumed that $F_0$ is the base change of $F$ along $\mathrm{res}_R$ (`hBC`), that $F$ satisfies `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic (maximalIdeal R) q x₀ x₁` (`hDr`), that $\mathfrak m_R = (x_0, x_1)$ (`hmax`), and (`huniv`) that $(R, F, x_0, x_1)$ is universal in the following sense: for every artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T$ with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ with kernel $\mathfrak m_T$ extending $\mathrm{res}_0$, every commutative formal group $G$ over $T$ which is the base change of $F_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_T$, and all $y_0, y_1 \in \mathfrak m_T$ with `G.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic (maximalIdeal T) q y₀ y₁`, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : R \to T$ with $\mathrm{res}_T \circ \varphi = \mathrm{res}_R$ for which there exist a formal group $F'$ over $T$ that is the base change of $F$ along $\varphi$ and a law isomorphism $\psi : F' \to G$ whose series has $n$-th coefficient reducing to $1$ for $n = 1$ and to $0$ otherwise, and with $\psi$ sending $\varphi(x_0) \mapsto y_0$ and $\varphi(x_1) \mapsto y_1$ under `appAdic` for $\mathfrak m_T$.
--
--   Finally, let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hγ`) and let $\rho_\gamma$ be an automorphism of the moduli problem (an action on points, natural in the $A_0$-algebra and preserving the $j$-invariant). The pinning hypothesis `hpin` identifies $\rho_\gamma$ on field-valued points: for every field $T$ that is an $A_0$-algebra and all raw objects $y, y'$ over $T$ with `IsUnit y.level.2.2.curve.Δ`, if $y'$ has the same curve as $y$ and the same $\Gamma_0$-slot `level.1`, if the point `toPoint` attached to $(x_P, y_P)$ of $y'$ on the base change of $y$'s curve equals $\gamma_{00}$ times the corresponding point of $y$, if $x_Q = x_P$ and $y_Q = y_P$ in the $\Gamma_1$-slot of $y'$, and if the Drinfeld-pair slot of $y'$ is the $\gamma$-relabelling `RawDrinfeldPair.relabel 𝒢 γ y.level.2.2 hΔ`, whose sections are the $\mathbb Z$-linear combinations $\gamma_{00}P + \gamma_{10}Q$ and $\gamma_{01}P + \gamma_{11}Q$ formed with $\mathcal G$, then $\rho_\gamma$ sends the class of $y$ to the class of $y'$. It is assumed that $\rho_\gamma$ acts trivially modulo $\mathfrak m_R$ on the classifying coordinates, $\iota(P_0.\mathrm{classify}(\rho_\gamma \cdot P_0.\mathrm{univ})(b)) - \iota(b) \in \mathfrak m_R$ for all $b \in B_0$ (`hfix`), and that $\theta_0 : R \to R$ is a $W_0$-algebra endomorphism with $\theta_0(\iota(b)) = \iota(P_0.\mathrm{classify}(\rho_\gamma \cdot P_0.\mathrm{univ})(b))$ for all $b$ (`hcompl`) and $\theta_0(r) - r \in \mathfrak m_R$ for all $r \in R$ (`hres`).
--
--   The last group of hypotheses compares the $\theta_0$-transport of the universal raw object with its $\gamma$-relabelling. Let $V$ be a variable change over $R$, let $\Delta$ of the Drinfeld-pair curve of `mapRing ι x` be a unit (`hΔ`), and let $x'$ be a raw object over $R$ with `act V (mapRing (θ₀.restrictScalars A₀) (mapRing ι x)) = x'` (`hact`). It is assumed that $x'$ has the same curve (`hcurve`) and the same $\Gamma_0$-slot (`hlev1`) as `mapRing ι x`, that the Drinfeld-pair slot of $x'$ is the $\gamma$-relabelling of that of `mapRing ι x` (`hlev22`), that over the fraction field of $R$ the point attached to the $\Gamma_1$-slot of $x'$ equals $\gamma_{00}$ times the point attached to the $\Gamma_1$-slot of `mapRing ι x` on the base change of the common curve (`hlev21`), and that in the $\Gamma_1$-slot of $x'$ one has $x_Q = x_P$ and $y_Q = y_P$ (`hlev21'`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is a conjunction of two congruences modulo $\mathfrak m_R^2$, written with the unit $u^{-1} = (V.u^{-1} : R^\times)$ of the variable change $V$ and the integer entries of $\gamma$ cast into $R$:
--   $$\theta_0(x_0) - u^{-1}\bigl(\gamma_{00}\,x_0 + \gamma_{10}\,x_1\bigr) \in \mathfrak m_R^2,$$
--   $$\theta_0(x_1) - u^{-1}\bigl(\gamma_{01}\,x_0 + \gamma_{11}\,x_1\bigr) \in \mathfrak m_R^2,$$
--   where $x_0 =$ `originParam χP` and $x_1 =$ `originParam χQ`.
--
--   This is the first-order reading of a $\Gamma_0(M')$-relabelling automorphism on the rigidified deformation ring of a supersingular moduli point with $\Gamma_0$-power, $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ and Drinfeld-basis level structure: on the two origin parameters of the universal Drinfeld pair, the induced endomorphism $\theta_0$ is given modulo $\mathfrak m_R^2$ by $u^{-1}$ times the linear substitution by $\gamma$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.exists_originParam_linearPart_of_algHom_comp_eq_classify_act_of_problemAut_relabel_rigidDataH1Pow_of_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.exists_originParam_linearPart_of_algHom_comp_eq_classify_act_of_problemAut_relabel_rigidDataH1Pow_of_mem_ssJSet), where the linear part of such an automorphism is extracted.
